ZX Spectrum core: GPL v3 for the core as a whole.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.


What is here. These files are MiSTer-devel/ZX-Spectrum_MiSTer (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/ZX-Spectrum_MiSTer), commit 33774ad
(2026-10-12), copied by tools/vendor_zx_mister.sh, unchanged except ula.sv, which gets tools/zx_ula.patch (the HBlank / HSync
statements of the 48K and the 128K in one pair, T119 5.15; the file says so at the place; SHA256SUMS lists the files as built). The terms are the ones written in each file's header:

  ula.sv            GPL v3 or later (Sorgelig, 2016)                       built with that one change (Timex, ULA+, Pentagon and the snow effect are
                                                                            tied off by the instance in cores/zx/trx/zx_core.v)
  ym2149.sv         BSD wording (MikeJ 2005, Sorgelig 2016-2019), no extra clause     built as it is
  T80/*.vhd         BSD wording (Daniel Wallner 2001-2002, MikeJ, Sorgelig 2018), no extra clause   source of cores/zx/gen/t80pa.v (below)

Not here, on purpose: rtl/keyboard.sv (its header adds "License is granted for non-commercial use only"), tape.sv, tzxplayer.vhd,
pzxplayer.sv, snap_loader.sv, turbosound.sv, the disk, SDRAM and sound extras, the MiSTer framework (sys/), and every ROM. The Spectrum's
48K and 128K ROMs are Amstrad's and never go into this repository, a bench, a package or a .cor: the app reads them at core start from the
user's files (roms: zx 48.rom, zx 128.rom), the benches from a path outside the tree or run a program written in the bench itself.

What is built is NOT only these files. cores/zx/gen/t80pa.v is what tools/zx_gen.sh makes of T80/ with GHDL (--synth --out=verilog, in a
container), plus two counted renames (the VHDL port name `do` is a SystemVerilog keyword; the instance `alu` and the signal ALU_Q would
collide in the Verilog), so that Verilator and Vivado read the same source. The BSD wording asks that the copyright notice and the
disclaimer are kept: they are in the VHDL in rtl/T80, which ships with the source, and in gen/t80pa.v's header.

What the licence means here. GPL v3 covers the gateware of this core and everything linked into its partial bitstream. A .cor or partial
bitstream of this core that is given to a third party has to come with its corresponding source: that is this directory (the upstream copy),
cores/zx/gen, cores/zx/trx, cores/zx/shared and cores/zx/layer2_zx.v (our glue), tools/vendor_zx_mister.sh, tools/zx_gen.sh and
tools/zxcpc_keys.py, and the build recipe cores/zx/mono/build_mono.tcl - all of it is in this repository. The host (layer 1), the other cores and the applications are separate works in separate partial bitstreams,
link nothing of this core and are not covered; host/ is not part of this core's build.
